turnip: darwin, the kernel's per-object limit (Query's max_bo_bytes, 256 MiB on Adreno830) is every layer's allocation limit

Adreno830's BoAlloc and BoImport refuse more than max_bo_bytes (kIOReturnBadArgument), while Turnip advertised maxMemoryAllocationSize
4 GiB - 1, maxBufferSize 4 GiB and images' maxResourceSize 4 GiB - 1: an 8192x8192 RGBA8 texture got as far as the kernel and the Metal
client saw an out-of-memory answer with a kernel BadArgument behind it. Now, on the native darwin path (not virtio-gpu):
- tu_physical_device.max_bo_size = Query's max_bo_bytes;
- VkPhysicalDeviceVulkan11Properties::maxMemoryAllocationSize, VkPhysicalDeviceVulkan13Properties::maxBufferSize and
  VkImageFormatProperties::maxResourceSize are capped at it;
- a BO or host import past it is refused before any kernel call (VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY / VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE), and
  named on stderr the first time and then every 10th, 100th, ...: "NativeAdreno: a BO of 257 MiB is past the kernel's per-object
  limit of 256 MiB (maxMemoryAllocationSize); refused (1 time)".
Against the tree after 0001-0003. MIT, as the files.

